🐛 Bug

To Reproduce
import torch

def script(fn):
    return torch.jit.script(fn)

def fn():
    def foo(x):
        return x
    def bar(x):
        return foo(x)

    ge = script(bar)

    x = torch.tensor(1.)
    y = foo(x)
    print(y)  

fn()


RuntimeError:
undefined value foo:
def bar(x):
    return foo(x)
           ~~~ <--- HERE

Environment
PT master

🐛 Bug
auto t=at::tensor({1});
t.requires_grad();
at::Error: requires_grad is not implemented for Tensor
this is deliberately inhibited in core/TensorImpl.h
not really a bug, but seems an innocent enough question for a tensor to ask of itself.
can go around via:
t.options().requires_grad();
but this doesn't get at the tensor's gradient setting:
inline TensorOptions Tensor::options() const {
 return TensorOptions().dtype(dtype())
                       .device(device())
                      .layout(layout())
                        .is_variable(is_variable());
}
creating via torch instead means requires_grad() is permitted:
auto v=torch::tensor({1.0}, at::requires_grad());
v.requires_grad();
but querying via options is misleading:
v.options().requires_grad();
will be always false
Additional context
(trying to sort out tensors from the at:: functions vs variables from torch:: in the new c++ api)

